{"id": "EUVD-2026-103335", "enisaUuid": "fcaededf-60b8-3c21-8316-7f0df7cca51c", "description": "phpMyFAQ before 4.1.9 and 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta does not require the current password when changing an account e-mail in the user control panel (UserController::updateData, api/user/data/update), checking only the session and CSRF token. An attacker with a hijacked session can set the e-mail to their own mailbox and use the password-reset flow to take over non-2FA accounts, including superadmin.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:18:30", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-7554-gx6g-xx77", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-before-4.1.9-and-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-missing-current-password-step-up-on-e-mail-change-enables-account-takeover"], "aliases": ["GHSA-ch92-qpmj-fc56", "CVE-2026-111884"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5b2622ec-82a1-3f75-865c-9ccab5ecacd6", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.1.9"}, {"id": "6ca1949e-553e-3028-ae00-45f103400be8", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ced26380-15f7-37bd-9e0d-48c78bf03a9d", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}